    "content": "Andrej Stojaković (born August 17, 2004) is the son of former NBA All-Star Peja Stojaković. A 6'7\" guard/forward, Andrej is a highly touted basketball player who has played for Stanford and California before transferring to the University of Illinois for the 2025-26 season. He is known as a talented scorer, previously a McDonald's All-American. Key Details About Andrej Stojaković: Background: Born in Greece to Peja and Aleka Kamila, he grew up in Carmichael, California, and attended Jesuit High School. College Career: Stanford (2023–2024): Played his freshman year for the Cardinal. Cal (2024–2025): Transferred to the California Golden Bears. Illinois (2025–present): Committed to the Fighting Illini in April 2025. Accomplishments: He was a 5-star recruit (according to the University of Illinois Athletics bio), a 2023 McDonald's All-American, a Jersey Mike's Naismith All-American, and participated in the Nike Hoop Summit. Playing Style: Described as a shooter with great pace, balance, and the ability to score off the dribble. Recent Status: As of late 2025, he has been navigating a knee injury while joining the Illinois program. Andrej is the eldest child of Peja Stojaković, who had a 13-year NBA career and won a championship with the Dallas Mavericks in 2011.",
